start your business part-time one of my  favorite strategies if you're just  getting started with your company and  start part-time don't go and quit your  job and jump into this company full-time  only to realize that three months later  you've run out of cash and have to go  back and beg for your job this comes as  a result of a question from Twitter  follower  Ahlan or who wrote in to say Evan can we  start a business while we're currently  working for other people and the answer  is absolutely now I've created a zuga  guide that walks you through kind of  step by step how to find the right  company to work for and then how to  actually get started on your own but let  me kind of summarize that entire guide  for you in some of the action steps for  you okay the first thing is if you're  going to be working for somebody if  you're gonna take a job you want a job  where you're gonna learn okay you don't  want a job just to make money  you want a job that's gonna teach you  the skills you need to be a better  entrepreneur and get a job at a company  that does a small company somebody who  you want to be in a few years somebody  who has maybe ten employees where you  can get close to the entrepreneur and  you can learn from them and you could  take on more projects every entrepreneur  is stressed out needs people to help  them needs good people and if you are  motivated dedicated employee who comes  and says hey I'd like to help out with  something else with more they're gonna  give you responsibilities  okay get closer entreprenuer the  business learn the ropes it's important  because if you do just go out and start  your company you're probably not gonna  last because too many entrepreneurs just  run out of cash they run out of money  and they have to go back and get their  old job better to realize that starting  the business takes time you need time  for momentum to build and to grow and  you can do that part-time while you  still are having a job and getting paid  and use the knowledge connections  experience that you get from your job  and make you better when you launch your  company the great thing about working  for somebody else while you're launching  your business is you're getting paid to  make mistakes you're getting paid by  somebody else to not only learn the  business  but to also make your mistakes you're  making mistakes working for somebody  else so that when you go and do your own  thing you dramatically reduce the number  of mistakes you're gonna make when it's  really important right when it's for you  the other thing it will teach you is is  this business for you or not a lot of  entrepreneurs start a business and they  think this is going to be a great idea  and then once they get into it they  realize I really shouldn't have done  that you know I'm not loving and it  wasn't what I thought it was gonna be  and so you can really reduce your risk  and and how much money you're spending  by going out and getting the job in the  field learn how the field works and see  if you like it see if this is still  something that you want to do because  even if you have huge energy and  excitement at the beginning you never  know until you actually get into it so  try it and and working for somebody for  six months or a year is not going to  kill you you've been doing it your whole  life okay it will not kill you to do  another six or 12 months working for  somebody who you admire who you like  who's doing something important who  you're learning from who's paying you to  gain experience connections contacts so  when you launch your business you'll be  ready to go and take on the world so  there's nothing wrong with working for  somebody else while you're launching  your business and I actually highly  recommend it believe who's be watching  like the video please give a thumbs up  below let me know what you think leave a  comment you have a question if it below  make a video response your feedback is  awesome for me 